## Reading

- `end=clogged`: the clog stop worked. The 60 s window fell from 138 mL (first window) to 21 mL (the last one, under 30 % of the first).
- Weighed 865 g against 673 mL counted: the flowmeter read about 78 % of the water. That is the low-flow under-read (F150). **The flow factor was not corrected:** the run ended `clogged` and F150 says the factor comes from a normal-flow run only.
- P max 3.56 bar, 0.04 bar under the 3.6 bar hard cap, with 465 pauses at the 3.35 bar pause level (F151). The cap was never tripped.
- The pressure pattern was the same as the used-filter runs of 2026-10-19: the flow fell from about 0.13 L/min at the start to 0.0 near the end.

## Verdict

**Diagnostic, not a pass.** The water (not clean) clogs a new filter at about 0.9 L, 865 g. Logged as a clog diagnostic (user, 2026-10-19). S1-B's own pass line (`end=volume`, 900–1100 g) is not met by this run.

Finding for the log: the clogging depends on the water, so an S1-B pass on dirty water may never happen. The stop criteria and the weighed partial volume are what S1-C needs.
